  "style": {
    "name": "Imperial Chinese memorial-hall — Cobalt Ascendant",
    "rationale": "Second pass: killed flat fields by carving the calcite into engaged corner piers, inter-bay pilasters, a recessed paneled podium belt with vertical ribs and gold string-courses; recessed the three vermilion doors behind raised calcite voussoir arches with gold keystones; added a repeating gold-tipped dougong bracket course carrying the eave; broke the wall with a gilded tablet plaque and three inscription panels. Held the document palette hard — dominant cobalt double roof (stepped for a true hip silhouette), calcite field, gold accents, vermilion heartbeat — so nothing drifts toward the reference's white."
